{
  "id": "COMPOUND:40444 - PROTEIN:5944",
  "verbalization": "Sansalvamide A is shown to have a target relationship with Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8 through multiple pathways, all of which involve the compound interacting with a class of molecules referred to as \"MIP\" (likely a metabolite or a related compound). These pathways indicate that Sansalvamide A acts as a target for a series of structurally diverse compounds, which in turn are targets of Mitogen-activated protein kinase kinase kinase 8. The evidence suggests that Sansalvamide A may exert its biological effects by interacting with these intermediates, which are subsequently processed by the kinase enzyme. The shared mechanism of action across these different molecular entities supports the idea that Sansalvamide A may influence the kinase activity through a common pathway, possibly by modulating the activity of the target molecules or by directly interacting with the kinase. The integration of these findings highlights a potential role for Sansalvamide A in modulating signaling pathways involving this kinase, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
